    "orthography writes initial l- as n-/y- and initial n- as y-, so 劉 is 류 mid-word but",
    "유 as a surname. Entries without it are unaffected by the rule.",
    "",
    "Pinyin is stored with tone marks. Tones are dropped for display but are what make",
    "the Wade-Giles/Yale derivation unambiguous, so do not strip them here."
